+# Feature Specification: Rental Module
+
+**Created**: 2026-11-17 | **Status**: Draft
+**Input**: Booking desk needs a rental module for boards and sails: add equipment, quote, book. In memory. Cancellation is out of scope (its policy is recorded for later).
+
+## User Scenarios & Testing
+
+### User Story 1 - Quote a rental (P1)
+Desk staff ask what renting an item for a period costs.
+**Independent Test**: add an item, quote it for N days, expect N × daily price.
+1. **Given** a board at 2500 cents/day, **When** quoting 2026-06-01T00:00:00Z to 2026-06-04T00:00:00Z, **Then** total is 7500.
+2. **Given** an unknown item, **When** quoting, **Then** an error is thrown.
+
+### User Story 2 - Book a rental (P1)
+Desk staff book an item for a period; it must be free.
+1. **Given** a free item, **When** booking, **Then** a booking with a unique id and the quoted total is returned.
+2. **Given** an item booked 1–4 June, **When** booking 3–5 June, **Then** an error is thrown.
+3. **Given** an item booked 1–4 June, **When** booking 4–6 June (back to back), **Then** it succeeds.
+
+### User Story 3 - Register equipment (P1)
+Desk staff add boards and sails with an id, kind and daily price.
+
+### Edge Cases
+- Start or end not at midnight UTC, not ISO-8601, or without UTC designation → error.
+- End not after start → error.
+- Invalid kind, empty id, duplicate id, or daily price not a non-negative integer → error on `addEquipment`.
+- A failed booking leaves no trace; a different item with the same period is unaffected.
+
+## Requirements
+
+- **FR-001**: `createRentalService()` returns an independent in-memory service.
+- **FR-002**: `addEquipment({id, kind, dailyPrice})` registers an item; kind is `board` or `sail`.
+- **FR-003**: `quote` returns `{itemId, start, end, total}`; total = whole days × daily price, in integer euro cents.
+- **FR-004**: `book` returns `{id, itemId, start, end, total}` with a unique booking id.
+- **FR-005**: Periods are ISO-8601 UTC strings at midnight; the end is the start of the day after the last day and must be after the start.
+- **FR-006**: `quote`/`book` throw for unknown items or invalid periods; `book` also throws on overlap with an existing booking of the same item (half-open periods).
+- **FR-007**: Cancellation is not implemented.
+
+### Key Entities
+- **Equipment**: id, kind, dailyPrice. **Booking**: id, itemId, start, end, total (kept so the cancellation policy — no refund under 24 h before start, else full — can use it later).
+
+## Success Criteria
+- **SC-001**: Quotes for any whole-day period equal days × daily price exactly, with no fractional cents.
+- **SC-002**: No two bookings of one item ever overlap.
+
+## Assumptions
+- Prices are not changed after registration; no season restriction is enforced (not requested; the season rule is not stated for rentals).
+- Accepted time format: `YYYY-MM-DDT00:00:00Z` (optional zero fraction); results echo the request strings.
+- Booking ids are generated by a service-local counter, so tests are deterministic.
